  "configuration_id": "config_048",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_036 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, weighted, singleprofile) at 0.537 acc, showing that scvi_n200 is a strong RNA encoder and weighted multimodal fusion provides a modest but consistent boost over RNA alone (0.520). However, the multiprofile dimension is completely untested—no experiment has yet explored whether aggregating multiple profiles improves performance. This is a high-uncertainty, high-impact design question. Question: config_048 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) directly extends config_036 by changing only the profile setting from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation, isolating the effect of multiprofile while holding the best-known encoder and fusion choices constant. Why this experiment: It is the single most informative next step because (1) it builds on the strongest evidence (scvi_n200 + vit_l + weighted), (2) it tests the largest unexplored design axis, (3) avgpool is a simple, interpretable aggregation that cleanly answers 'does multiprofile help?' before committing budget to more complex aggregations like transformer, and (4) a positive result would open an entire new optimization space, while a null result would efficiently rule out multiprofile as a priority."
}

